  "question": {
    "text": "A pendulum clock is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> fast at a temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> slow at a temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. At what temperature does it give the correct time? (take time interval = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>hours</mi></math>)",
    "image": null
